  "derivation_rationale": {
    "low_threshold_rationale": "Cutoff 0.40 maps to the ~96th percentile of legitimate transactions. Allows 96.00% of all traffic (54,676 legit transactions) to pass cleanly with straight-through processing, while filtering out 91.84% of all fraud into investigation or escalation queues.",
    "high_threshold_rationale": "Cutoff 0.75 maps to the ~99th percentile of legitimate transactions (p99 = 0.7553). Concentrates 89.80% of all fraud (88/98 cases) into the high-priority review band with a 13.15% fraud density, limiting clean customer friction to only 1.02% of legitimate traffic.",
    "medium_band_rationale": "Spans the 0.40 to 0.75 score window (2.82% of all traffic). Represents borderline, multi-signal transactions where anomaly flags exist but risk is not yet definitive, providing the ideal operational operating range for Phase 2 Evidence Agent investigation."
  },
